# CH15 — Light in the Flood. Bellharbor upper gallery: clear the upper route, move the residents, SC09.

@scene CH15_ARRIVE once
say narr | The upper gallery of the old archive annex. The roof sags over a shelter of families - held up by a lattice of white light.
say narr | Beneath it, standing in knee-deep water, Morwen. Her hands are raised. They are shaking.
say nera | Morwen!
say tessa | Don't come under the edge. The roof goes when I stop.
say jori | She's been holding it for three days. We bring her water. She won't sit.
say oriel | Then we get everyone out from under it first. The walkway above - is it passable?
say jori | Bales came down across it in the first quake. There are winches, but nobody's had the hands.
objective oriel | Clear the upper walkway with the two winches (west side passage), then lead the three families out along it.
@end

@scene CH15_TESSA
if flag:t04g_res1,flag:t04g_res2,flag:t04g_res3 ready
say tessa | Not yet. There are still people under here. Don't ask me to stop.
end
label ready
say tessa | ...Is that everyone?
@end

@scene CH15_JORI
say jori | Kids are ringing the alarm with a cooking pot since the ministry took the bells. Loudest thing in town.
@end

@scene CH15_WINCH1
if flag:t04g_clear1 done
sfx FX010
set t04g_clear1
say narr | The winch creaks. The first mass of rope-bales lifts off the walkway and swings clear.
end
label done
say narr | The west winch is holding the bales clear.
@end

@scene CH15_WINCH2
if flag:t04g_clear2 done
sfx FX010
set t04g_clear2
say narr | The second winch lifts the last bales. The walkway runs clear to the east stair.
end
label done
say narr | The east winch is holding the bales clear.
@end

@scene CH15_RES1
if flag:t04g_clear1,flag:t04g_clear2 go
say elder | The walkway's blocked. We tried. We'll wait for the young woman to finish whatever she's doing.
end
label go
say elder | Up the gap and along the walkway? At my age? ...Yes. Yes, all right. Take my arm.
fade out 0.3
set t04g_res1
fade in 0.3
call CH15_COUNT
@end

@scene CH15_RES2
if flag:t04g_clear1,flag:t04g_clear2 go
say survivor | We can't go through the water - my son can't swim. And the walkway's full of bales.
end
label go
say survivor | The walkway's clear? Then we're going. Thank you. Thank her.
fade out 0.3
set t04g_res2
fade in 0.3
call CH15_COUNT
@end

@scene CH15_RES3
if flag:t04g_clear1,flag:t04g_clear2 go
say child | I'm not scared. I'm waiting. It's different.
end
label go
say child | Is the lady going to be okay? ...Okay. I'll go if you count me.
say oriel | One. There. You are counted.
fade out 0.3
set t04g_res3
fade in 0.3
call CH15_COUNT
@end

@scene CH15_COUNT
if flag:t04g_res1,flag:t04g_res2,flag:t04g_res3 all
say narr | (Some families are still under the roof.)
end
label all
objective oriel | Everyone is out along the walkway. Go to Morwen.
@end

@scene CH15_SC09 once
say tessa | The roof goes when I stop.
say nera | Nobody is under it now.
say tessa | There could be -
say oriel | We counted them. Twice.
say dain | Let it go.
say tessa | I do not know what happens after.
say jori | We light the lamps.
music silence
wait 0.4
flash #ffffff
say narr | Morwen lowers her hands. The lattice goes out. The roof comes down into empty water with a long, tired sound.
fade out 0.8
wait 0.6
say narr | Darkness. Then, one by one along the walkway, ordinary lanterns - held by the families she was protecting.
fade in 0.8
music M003
say tessa | ...Oh.
say tessa | They did that. Not me.
say nera | You can sit down now, Morwen.
say tessa | I can sit down.
say tessa | The Golem. We have to find the Golem. I want to see a machine that runs without someone pretending to be its fuel.
join C02
chapter CH15
objective dain | Travel to Cinderwake (north-west, beyond Rootward) and find the Golem.
rumor | Cinderwake crews are rotating heat between workshops with waterwheels. Someone says the Golem is in the old assembly yard.
level_floor 27
@end

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Bellharbor upper town (post)
@scene T04U_JORI
if ch:CH15 after
say jori | Morwen's in the upper gallery. She won't let go of the roof. Please - she'll listen to you before she listens to me.
end
label after
if ch:CH20 q
say jori | The lower streets are gone, but the ropewalks make good roads. We're painting names on every door that has someone behind it.
end
label q
say jori | Sak - if you see him - tell him I have people who need their names fixed. The right way this time.
@end

@scene T04U_POT
say child | CLANG! That's the alarm. They took the bells so I use the pot. CLANG! That one was for practice.
@end

@scene T04U_CHAPEL
say monk | The tide chapel is an evacuation station now. We ring for boats, not for prayers. Both get answered about as often.
@end

@scene T04U_SHOP
say keeper | Charts! Old charts, useless. New charts, useful but wrong. Buy both and average them.
shop SHOP_T04
@end

@scene T04U_ROPE
say worker | The ropewalks were for making rope. Now they're the only roads above water. Rope's still useful, mind.
@end

@scene T04U_SAILOR
say sailor | Manifests used to list refugees as 'cargo'. Now we list cargo as 'refugees' so nobody steals it. Joke. Mostly.
@end

@scene T04U_INN
say monk | Hammocks in the chapel loft. Free for anyone who pulls a shift on the pumps. You look like you'd pull a shift.
inn 0
@end
